ically loaded into a training pipeline without inspection, where a missing column or a value such as \texttt{age="sixty"} either stops the job or is silently turned into a missing value. Moreover, datasets of different sizes cannot be compared fairly across generators or runs, nor exchanged between facilities in an agreed format. A generator that violates these constraints thus corrupts the training data without the user noticing. In addition, each request to a commercial LLM has a monetary cost, proportional to the tokens (word fragments) processed, which is rarely reported.
 
